{"user": "Why do those diagonals get flipped?", "user_ts": "2026-08-07T14:50:37.359599+00:00", "assistant": "Diagonals work just like rows/columns in Othello.\n\nA line flips only if it is:\n\n**your new disc \u2192 continuous opponent discs \u2192 your existing disc**\n\nSo if Black plays **g2**, then White may be able to play **h1**:\n\n**h1 White \u2192 g2 Black \u2192 f3 White**\n\nThat sandwiches your **g2** disc diagonally, so **g2 flips to White**. The key is the line must be unbroken \u2014 no empty squares or same-color disc in the middle.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-07T14:50:48.204984+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-07T14:50:50.283538+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Worked Line", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Worked Line", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Worked Line": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Local Justification": 1}, "confidence": {"Worked Line": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Local Justification": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Worked Line", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Worked Line", "General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min